WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W15 (0.2.1)


STATE

  Version 0.2.1, Phase P3 IN PROGRESS (line editor and history complete),
  on branch dev. 0.2.1 adds:
  - append-only command history in include/tam-clam/history.h and
    src/history/history.c: single-write O_APPEND records with timestamp,
    exit status, and cwd (default via libtam tam_xdg_path, overridable
    with HISTFILE), damage-tolerant reader, live sync across concurrent
    shells, `--private` mode, leading-space ignore, and `history`
    builtin;
  - line-editor integration in src/edit/edit.c: Up/Down prefix-filtered
    history navigation, Ctrl+F live incremental search overlay (Ctrl+F /
    Alt+N next, Alt+Shift+N prev, Enter accepts into buffer, Esc cancels),
    and Alt+L insert-last-arg with repeat cycling;
  - tests/test_history.c (round-trip, damaged/truncated recovery,
    concurrent O_APPEND writers, /dev/full, private mode), extended
    tests/pty/test_pty.c, and sandbox/demo-0.2.1-history.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


